<Layout title="About — MimicryDB"><div class="container py-12"><h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">About MimicryDB</h1><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl">MimicryDB is designed as durable scientific infrastructure for documenting mimic–model interactions across the Tree of Life. Every published claim requires provenance linking an interaction to references and evidence passages — <em>no claim without provenance</em>.</p><h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">What is a mimicry interaction?</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">The fundamental record is directional: <strong>Mimic → Model | Receiver</strong>. A hoverfly resembles an ant to a predator; an orchid flower mimics a female bee to attract pollinating males. Records keep publication, interaction, taxon pair, and evolutionary origin strictly separate, and mark knowledge as <em>reported</em>, <em>supported</em>, or <em>inferred</em>.</p><h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">How records are curated</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">Records move through <span class="pill">candidate</span> → <span class="pill">draft</span> → <span class="pill">needs review</span> → <span class="pill">reviewed</span> → <span class="pill">published</span>. External contributors cannot publish directly; suggestions arrive via issues or the candidate inbox and are vetted by curators. Every scientific change is audit-logged with its reason. See <a href="https://github.com/ZyYang0124/MimicryDB/blob/main/docs/CURATION_GUIDE.md">docs/CURATION_GUIDE.md</a>.</p><h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Evidence first</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">Each record carries an evidence grade E0–E4 with a written justification. Reporting a resemblance is not equivalent to demonstrating mimicry — the framework keeps that distinction explicit. See the <a href="/MimicryDB/evidence/">evidence grades</a>.</p><h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Status</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl">Alpha prototype (v0.3.0). The current website uses clearly labeled sample records while the normalized Supabase schema and curation workflow are developed. Demo data is never presented as curated science, and statistics derived from it are labeled as such.</p><p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl">Design references and the longer-term roadmap (live database, LLM literature mining with human curation, phylogenetic layers, versioned data releases) are documented in <a href="https://github.com/ZyYang0124/MimicryDB/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md">docs/ROADMAP.md</a>.</p></div></Layout>
